#
# The kidnapped-robot problem: teleport the body without telling the
# localizer, so AMCL's estimate is suddenly, genuinely wrong and has to
# recover from its own observations.
#
# Served as /faults/kidnap by ral_faults/fault_manager.py (Phase 4.4).
# Injection point: /world/<world>/set_pose (gz entity pose). Nothing touches
# /initialpose or /amcl_pose - resetting the filter would stage the recovery
# instead of demonstrating it.
#
# `new_pose` is in the gz WORLD frame, like every other gz entity pose, and is
# NOT converted through world_to_map.
#
# Wheel odometry is continuous across the teleport (the wheels did not turn),
# which is exactly the discontinuity the estimator must survive. Metrics
# computed from ground truth must exclude the teleport step itself from path
# length; metrics.py does that explicitly and reports the excluded distance.

geometry_msgs/Pose new_pose
---
bool success
string message
